        "payload": "tree 00d1b36d001423fb65c6becfc83141252a712e30\nparent 3a10b5b5f0a7586df8928d580a3009744ebb2079\nauthor leoca <leo.camus23@gmail.com> 1790671783 +0000\ncommitter leoca <leo.camus23@gmail.com> 1790671783 +0000\n\nBIP-346: fix two-byte individual index parsing in reference impl\n\nIn individual selection mode the BIP says that when an index byte has its\nhighest bit set, \"the remaining 7 bits, together with the next byte's 8\nbits represent the index\". parse_inout_selection masked that byte with\n(1 << 7) instead of with its complement, so it kept only the flag bit and\nthrew away the seven value bits: every two-byte index evaluated to\n0x8000 + next_byte.\n\nIn absolute mode that is always out of bounds, so a perfectly valid\nselector using the two-byte encoding is rejected. In relative mode\nread_i15 masks 0x8000 away again, so offsets of 256 or more collapse to\ntheir low 8 bits and silently select a different input than the one the\nselector names.\n\nThe committed test vectors are unaffected: generate_vectors only\nexercises single-byte indices (see its TODO about needing more than 32\nin/outputs), and txhash_vectors.json regenerates byte for byte. Added a\ntest asserting that both encodings of the same absolute index produce the\nsame TxHash.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNPivv4DtV9q4oea5XsNOpfD3zZ\n9EZyXLJd5WA3dO4nIAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFBGA7QBo695HbzjIjD3fEFqiiJP16HZAlNbJKO/pmmkb6wgL+m00/GO4HQgURmIqi\nYVefxWMTsJfpMWdw53GQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----"
