      "body": "Tested ACK 58de753. I added a relative-mode case next to yours: index -1 written in one byte (`0x7f`) and in two bytes (`0xff 0xff`). Both now give the same hash. On master the two-byte form fails with \"selected index out of bounds\".\n\nWhile testing I noticed three places where the BIP text disagrees with the code. Relative indices run from -16384 to +16383, not -16382. The absolute and relative mode bullets say \"second highest bit\", but the flag is the third highest bit, as the line above them says. A 5-bit count allows at most 31 individually selected items, not 32.\n",
