      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Thanks for the update. I ran the reference implementation at 3ff55fe.\n\n`cargo test` in `bip-0346/ref-impl` passes: 2 passed, 0 failed. `two_byte_relative_index_matches_single_byte` is one of them.\n\nWith the parser line reverted to master's (`first & (1 << 7)`), both tests fail. The relative test gets `Ok(0xf405c325...)` for `0x7f` and `Err(\"selected index out of bounds\")` for `0xff 0xff`, so it does catch the bug.\n\nThe test encodes -1 from input 1 as `0x7f` and as `0xff 0xff` and compares the two hashes, as intended.\n\nThe text now matches the code: third highest bit, -16384..+16383, and 31 individually selected items (the 5-bit count maximum). I found no other number in the individual-selection section that disagrees with the parser.\n\nCI on 3ff55fe is green.\n\nTested ACK 3ff55fe.\n",
